From 66f60d503120c3578cc2503d7c2da477d68e4f6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Geerinck <xavier.geerinck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:28:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] fix(sandbox): context-aware turn wait; review minors

Calls now wait for their turn on a 1-slot channel semaphore that also
selects on the caller's context and on a per-target closed channel, so a
caller that gives up or a removed target no longer blocks behind a long
exec, and a dead context never reaches the driver. Also: halt under the
factory lock, Closed errors carry the actor method, prebuilt lost error,
New rejects a nil driver, and tests no longer require off the test
goroutine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
